{% doc %}
  A script module that loads later instead of with the page, so it doesn't
  compete with the first screen's styles, fonts and images.
  assets/lazy-modules.js imports it:
  - `visible` (default): once its section comes within a screen of the viewport;
  - `idle`: once the page has loaded and the browser is idle, or on the
    visitor's first interaction, whichever comes first.
  In the theme editor everything loads right away.

  Use it for components below the first screen and for things that only
  matter once the visitor acts (drawers, modals, hover effects). Keep a plain
  `<script type="module">` for what the first screen needs to work.

  @param {string} src - Asset file name, e.g. 'video-carousel.js'.
  @param {string} [on] - When to load: 'visible' (default) or 'idle'.

  @example
  {% render 'lazy-script', src: 'video-carousel.js' %}
{% enddoc %}

<template data-lazy-module="{{ src | asset_url }}" data-load-on="{{ on | default: 'visible' }}"></template>
